# ============================================================================
# Operation Vault — environment
# ============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never
# put a real key here.
#
# IMPORTANT, and the thing that will silently waste an hour if you get it
# wrong: this is a VITE app, not Next.js. Only variables prefixed `VITE_` are
# exposed to browser code. A `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable will be `undefined` at
# runtime with no error, and the app will quietly fall back to offline mode.
# ============================================================================

# --- Supabase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
#
# Leave BOTH of these unset to run the game offline: mock questions,
# localStorage progress, bot leaderboard, no network. That is the normal way to
# work on screens, and nothing breaks — see src/lib/supabase.ts.
#
# The anon key is meant to be public. It is safe in a client bundle because
# every table is behind row-level security and every scoring decision happens
# in a SECURITY DEFINER function. Do not put the service_role key here, or
# anywhere else in this repo — it bypasses all of that.
VITE_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co"
VITE_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="YOUR-ANON-KEY"

# --- Gemini -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the art pipeline only (src/art/README.md), never at runtime by the
# game. AI Studio injects this automatically when the applet runs there.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# --- Hosting ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this is served from. Used for self-referential links; injected
# automatically in AI Studio.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"
